# Every path routes to the repository owner, who is reviewer of record for all work
# produced by both agents.
#
# AGENTS.md §2 is the single source of truth for ownership zones. This file encodes that
# same map as literal paths because GitHub cannot read a table; if the two ever disagree,
# AGENTS.md is right and this file is stale. The zone comments below are NOT decoration —
# they record which agent owns which directory. GitHub cannot enforce that split today
# because both agents push through the same account, so the zones are enforced by the PR
# checklist and by review, and this file exists to route the review.
#
# When either agent gets its own GitHub identity, replace the handle on that agent's
# lines and turn on "Require review from Code Owners" in branch protection. Note that
# GitHub never requests review from a PR's own author, so code-owner enforcement only
# becomes meaningful once author and owner can differ.

